README.md:11:Open `http://localhost:8080`. The server binds to `0.0.0.0`; `PORT` defaults to 8080 and `DB_PATH` defaults to `./data/workboard.sqlite`. Keep the configured SQLite file to preserve projects, archive state, tasks, and completion state across restarts. Existing databases are automatically upgraded with active projects, Normal task priorities, and Normal project defaults, empty task due dates and notes, and live task deletion state without changing existing task data. Its parent directory is created automatically.
README.md:37:## Task directory
README.md:39:`Task directory` on the home page opens `/directory`, a read-only view across projects. Each opening starts with Active project scope, All task and priority filters, and empty due range and title search. Scope, live/deleted completion, priority, inclusive due range, and normalized title-only search intersect without modifying data. Invalid ranges preserve the applied range and results. Rows show the original owner, title, completion, priority, due date, and literal multiline notes, in project creation order and remembered task order. `Open project` opens the owner with default project filters; `Projects` returns to the home page. Archived and deleted tasks remain readable without editable row controls.
